@startuml client_connection_lifetime_transaction_activity
title ClientConnectionLifetime - lifetime-only transaction

start
:ExecuteTransaction(actor);
:Lock mutex_;
:Create Operation under that lock;
if (Operation admitted?) then (yes)
    :Execute actor(descriptor_) through Operation::Execute;
    note right
        The operation unlocks for actor execution and relocks afterward.
        It remains registered through the transaction's final continuation.
    end note
    :Retain the expected-result actor value;
else (no)
    :Select EINVAL without invoking the actor;
endif
:End Operation scope under the mutex;
:Unlock mutex_;
:Return the actor result or admission error;
stop

legend
    This helper never examines the send FIFO or ordinary reply reservation.
    It permits future explicitly selected native request/reply transactions.
    No native engine transaction capability or configuration option is added.
    Descriptor retirement still waits for the operation to terminate.
endlegend

@enduml